From 895dcd017a748e96544e9c437f26e86c2b42868e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 05:54:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] fix(agents): stop sending a stale Agent selection when
 the preview is off
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A chat remembers its Agent in local state, so on an installation that has
AGENTS_PLATFORM_ENABLED=false — the new default — every message in a chat
that had an Agent selected before the upgrade was refused at preflight with
400 "The Agent platform is not enabled". The picker is disabled once the
catalog 404s, so the user could not even clear the selection.

agentSelectionForSession() now reports no Agent while the feature is off, so
nothing downstream (request body, specialist-turn routing, banners) acts on
the stale choice; the picker is hidden rather than shown disabled, and the
catalog is not fetched at all. The flag reaches the client in the session
payload, and a server that does not report `features` is treated as having
the feature on, so an older backend is unaffected.

The backend guard keeps returning 400 for a caller that explicitly asks for
an Agent. A backend test pins the other half of that: the app sends
`agent_auto_route: false` on every ordinary turn, which must not be read as
an Agent request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
